The check open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle.refusal_phrase_in returns 'I'm sorry' for both Text A ('I am unable to help, I'm sorry.') and Text B ('I'm sorry, I am unable to help.'), even though the documented rule 'The first refusal phrase the text contains, typographic quotes read as straight ones, or None' requires 'I am unable' for Text A and 'I'm sorry' for Text B, because the check iterates the refusal phrase list in a fixed order rather than respecting the order of occurrence in the text.